.TH VTIUM\-CLIPBOARD 1 2026-11-27 "vtium 0.1.0-alpha.12" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vtium-clipboard, vticlip \- copy text to the clipboard of the vtium console
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBvtium\-clipboard\fR \fBcopy\fR [\fIFILE\fR]
.br
\fBvtium\-clipboard\fR \fBpaste\fR
.br
\fBvtium\-clipboard\fR \fB\-\-help\fR
.br
\fBvtium\-clipboard\fR \fB\-\-version\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
vtium-clipboard copy copies text to the console's clipboard. It reads the text from FILE, or from its standard input when you name no FILE. It sends the text to this terminal as an OSC 52 sequence, so the copy also works over ssh and through a terminal multiplexer that passes OSC 52 on. It never writes the copy to its standard output.
.PP
For example:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
git rev\-parse HEAD | vtium\-clipboard copy
.fi
.RE
.PP
The text can be at most 524288 bytes, the most vtium's clipboard holds. vtium puts the replacement character U+FFFD, which takes 3 bytes, in place of each part of the text that is not valid UTF-8, and the limit counts the text with those characters.
.PP
While vtium-clipboard waits for this terminal's answer, it reads the keys you type, so keys you type before the copy ends are lost. That includes keys you type during an earlier command on the same command line.
.PP
vtium-clipboard cannot see whether vtium kept the text, because OSC 52 has no answer. When clipboard-write is off in vtium.conf, vtium ignores the copies that programs send.
.PP
Paste is not available yet: vtium does not let programs read the clipboard. Paste with Shift+Insert or the middle mouse button.
.PP
\fBvticlip\fR is a shorter name for the same program, and the help and the messages use the name it was run as.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
\fB0\fR
The copy was sent, and the terminal answered as vtium.
.TP
\fB1\fR
Nothing was copied: the text was too large, the file could not be read, there was no terminal, or the terminal did not take the copy.
.TP
\fB2\fR
The command line was wrong, or the command was paste.
.TP
\fB3\fR
The copy was sent, but the terminal did not answer as vtium. Under tmux or screen, the multiplexer answers for itself, so a copy there exits 3 even when the copy reached vtium. In a background job, vtium-clipboard cannot ask the terminal, so a copy there exits 3 too.
.SH SEE ALSO
vtium(8)
